4. Attack surface: every OTHER writer of StartDate.
   - `grep -rn "\.StartDate = " internal --include=*.go` (non-test) finds
     exactly two persisted-plan writers: settings_current_month.go:105
     (resolveCurrentMonth, pre-existing, shifts via the same
     shiftScheduleOffsets) and settings.go:1461 (this task's new manual
     path, now also shifting). No third writer.
   - `applySettingsUpdates`'s `updates` map (used by both
     UpdateSettingsWithPersons and the persons-less UpdateSettings) has no
     "start_date" key handled anywhere -> UpdateSettings (the non-Persons
     path) structurally cannot move StartDate.
   - MCP `apply_changes` -> `ApplyOverrides` -> `overrides.Apply`: the
     `overrides.Overrides` struct (internal/services/retirement/overrides)
     has no StartDate field at all -> cannot move StartDate, no
     double-writer risk from the MCP surface.
   - chain.go's `prepareChainedSettings` sets `prepared.StartDate =
     primary.StartDate` directly with no shift, but this builds an
     EPHEMERAL engine-input struct for a scenario-chain transition (never
     goes through SettingsManager.saveInternal, never persisted) and is
